        "description": "Open field. Motes and Drifters, and nothing else — no Suppressor, no punctuation of any kind. A Suppressor switches the player's Engine off, and the tutorial room is where somebody is still learning that they have an Engine at all; a mechanic that reads as the game being broken is the worst possible first lesson. The gate siege is where they meet one, and it arrives from the other side of the door with The Sink's roster, which is exactly the right introduction: the room you are about to enter, showing you what it has. The one room that stops: Threat 6 is about five minutes in, and past it The Heap holds — same composition, same density, same punctuation, forever. Long enough to die a few times and work out a strategy; flat enough that farming it is a decision to stop earning. The run's Threat keeps climbing behind the door.",
